Inventory graph|ansible-inventory -i inventory.yml --graph|Resolves inventory and displays group membership.|Review the exact fleet before running a play.|Group branches show membership; unexpected hosts indicate inventory or filter problems.|@web: ... host1 ... host2|Read-only discovery may call external inventory APIs; inspect a trusted inventory source.
Host variables|ansible-inventory -i inventory.yml --host HOST|Prints resolved inventory variables for one host.|Find connection settings or unexpected variable values.|JSON keys show inventory-derived values, not every later play-level override.|{"ansible_host":"192.0.2.10"}|Can reveal secrets; replace HOST and protect output.
List play targets|ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml site.yml --list-hosts|Lists hosts matched by each play without executing its tasks.|Verify host patterns and limits before changes.|Read the play name, pattern and host count for every play.|hosts (2): host1 host2|Inventory plugins may execute discovery; use trusted project files.
List tasks|ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml site.yml --list-tasks|Shows statically discoverable tasks selected by a playbook.|Review order and scope before execution.|Dynamic includes may not expose every eventual task in this view.|tasks: Install package ... Configure service ...|Does not execute normal tasks; not a complete prediction of dynamic behavior.
Syntax validation|ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml site.yml --syntax-check|Parses and checks playbook syntax.|Catch malformed YAML and structural issues early.|Success normally prints the playbook name; failures identify parsing context.|playbook: site.yml|Does not validate every runtime variable, remote command or application configuration.
Check mode|ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml site.yml --check --limit CANARY|Requests predicted changes on a limited target set.|Preview supported operations before a real rollout.|changed means a predicted change for supporting modules; skipped tasks may reduce coverage.|PLAY RECAP ... changed=1 failed=0|Not a universal dry run; modules and tasks can have exceptions, so review trusted content and use a safe canary.
Check with diff|ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml site.yml --check --diff --limit CANARY|Adds supported before/after diffs to check-mode output.|Review rendered configuration changes.|Lines prefixed - are removed and + are added; inspect paths and values.|--- before ... +++ after|Diffs can expose secrets; disable diff on sensitive tasks.
Module documentation|ansible-doc ansible.builtin.template|Displays the installed module's options, behavior and examples.|Confirm parameters and check-mode support for the actual installed version.|Read required fields, attributes and return values before using conditions.|OPTIONS ... ATTRIBUTES ... RETURN VALUES|Local read-only documentation lookup.
Collection versions|ansible-galaxy collection list|Lists installed collections and versions.|Reproduce a controller environment and diagnose version differences.|Multiple installation paths may contain different versions; note the path headings.|Collection Version ... ansible.posix ...|Read-only; compare with project requirements.
Connectivity test|ansible -i inventory.yml CANARY -m ansible.builtin.ping|Tests Ansible connection and Python execution on selected hosts.|Distinguish transport or interpreter problems from playbook logic.|pong means module execution succeeded; unreachable indicates connection-level failure.|HOST SUCCESS => {"ping":"pong"}|Not ICMP ping; runs a module on the authorized target.
Gather selected facts|ansible -i inventory.yml CANARY -m ansible.builtin.setup -a 'filter=ansible_distribution*'|Collects filtered operating-system facts.|Check platform assumptions used by roles.|Returned ansible_facts show distribution and version fields available on the host.|"ansible_distribution": "Debian"|Runs read-oriented fact gathering remotely; scope targets and protect inventory details.
List tags|ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml site.yml --list-tags|Shows tags available for task selection.|Understand supported partial-run entry points.|TASK TAGS identifies selectable labels; dependencies may still be omitted by selective execution.|TASK TAGS: [config, packages]|Read-only task discovery; test tag combinations before production use.
